# Keep local build output out of the image build context.
#
# Both targets install their own dependencies (`npm ci` in web-deps, `dotnet restore` in
# engine-builder). Without these exclusions, running `dotnet build` or `npm install` here
# before `docker compose up --build` ships a few hundred MB of host-specific output into
# the context — and, worse, `COPY dotnet/ ./` would drop a stale obj/project.assets.json
# with absolute host paths into the builder stage and break the in-container restore.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/bin
**/obj
.git
.vs
.vscode
